Feature: The rules of answers, stored records and events
  Each value is checked alone, as the harness checks an answer of the core or the shell checks a stored record.

  Scenario Outline: An object without a required property is rejected
    When I check a "<definition>" with:
      | <property> |
      |            |
    Then the value is rejected by "required" of "<definition>"

    Examples:
      | definition             | property          |
      | accepted_transfer      | new_ticket        |
      | cancelled_event        | event_id          |
      | entry_result           | verdict           |
